AI Secure Controls Framework: how to continue the mapping

What changed
The framework is updated as a draft and extra details are removed for now. Two columns are added: Subdomain (from Rashi's domain/subdomain structure) and AI use case.

Steps (repeat for each domain)

Filter the Domain column to one domain.
Map subdomains. Give the AI tool the filtered requirements (ID, name, description) and Rashi's subdomains for that domain, and ask it to propose a subdomain for each requirement.
Verify. This is mandatory. Check every row against the description and correct it, then fill in the Subdomain column. Leave a comment on anything unclear.
Map AI use cases. Use the AI tool the same way, based on the requirement descriptions and the 5 categories below.
Verify and fill in the AI use case column.

AI use case categories (working definitions)

Productivity AI: vendor AI assistants for employees (M365 Copilot, Amazon Quick)
Developer AI: AI coding tools (GitHub Copilot, Kiro, Claude Code)
Vendor Integrated AI: AI inside third-party SaaS; TMCC doesn't control the model
Agentic AI: AI taking actions via tools/APIs (Copilot Studio agents, MCP)
Generative AI: custom apps on AWS Bedrock via the AI gateway

Conventions

Don't change requirement text or IDs.
